+You are reviewing a plan before it is built, in the Spideryarn repo (this working tree). Read-only: do not edit any file.
+
+The plan: docs/plans/261025b-the-chrome-extension-findable-from-help-the-command-bar-and-a-refused-import.md
+The ask it answers: docs/project/chrome-extension.md § What it does not do yet → Being found, and Greg's brief: make the Chrome extension findable from /help, the command bar and above all the import flow when a pasted address hits a site that turns our server away; signal it, do not push it; every place takes the store link from PRODUCTION_EXTENSION_ID in src/web/extension-handoff.ts (null today); while null each place shows nothing (or Help text without a broken link); when the id arrives, setting that constant must be the ONLY change needed.
+
+Read the code the plan touches before judging: src/web/extension-handoff.ts, src/web/UploadInstead.tsx, src/web/SavePageBookmarklet.tsx, src/web/AddPage.tsx (around UploadInstead), src/messages.ts (SUGGESTS_UPLOAD, the fetch failure sentences and codes), src/web/help/help-markdown.tsx (tokens, drawBlock, plainBlock, expandHelpTokens, targetOf), src/web/help/pages/adding-articles.md, tests/help-corpus.test.ts, src/web/CommandBar.tsx (besideTheModes, helpRow, APP_PAGES), tests/command-pick-catalogue.test.ts, tests/command-match-arguments.test.ts, docs/project/help-page.md.
+
+Look hard for: anything that would make the Overseer's one-line change insufficient (another generated/committed file or test that depends on the id; a snapshot); anything that would draw a broken or dead link while null; the right subset of failure codes for SUGGESTS_EXTENSION (read each code's sentence — which failures would the extension, which captures the page as the reader's own browser renders it, actually get round?); whether the store URL form is right; security (an off-site link from our pages, new tab handling); and whether the "corpus is always empty for the token" trade-off is the right call versus the alternatives listed. Also say if anything is simpler.
+
+Answer with a verdict (GO / GO WITH CHANGES / REWORK) and numbered findings, each with severity, evidence (file:line) and the concrete fix.
